{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"final","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"scale","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vector2","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiftGodotRuntime7Vector2V"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"set","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This property is mainly intended to be used for animation purposes. To support multiple resolutions in your project, use an appropriate viewport stretch mode as described in the "},{"type":"text","text":"documentation"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of scaling Controls individually."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Note"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/FontFile\/oversampling","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" does "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" take "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control\/scale","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" into account. This means that scaling up\/down will cause bitmap fonts and rasterized (non-MSDF) dynamic fonts to appear blurry or pixelated. To ensure text remains crisp regardless of scale, you can enable MSDF font rendering by enabling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProjectSettings\/gui\/theme\/defaultFontMultichannelSignedDistanceField"},{"type":"text","text":" (applies to the default project font only), or enabling "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Multichannel Signed Distance Field"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" in the import options of a DynamicFont for custom fonts. On system fonts, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/SystemFont\/multichannelSignedDistanceField","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" can be enabled in the inspector."}]}],"name":"Note"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the Control node is a child of a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Container","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" node, the scale will be reset to "},{"code":"Vector2(1, 1)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when the scene is instantiated. To set the Control’s scale when it’s instantiated, wait for one frame using "},{"code":"await get_tree().process_frame","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" then set its "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control\/scale","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" property."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Note"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/control\/scale"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control"]]},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"scale","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vector2","preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiftGodotRuntime7Vector2V","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"externalID":"s:10SwiftGodot7ControlC5scale0aB7Runtime7Vector2Vvp","modules":[{"name":"SwiftGodot"}],"symbolKind":"property","title":"scale"},"abstract":[{"text":"The node’s scale, relative to its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"size"},{"text":". Change this property to scale the node around its ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control\/pivotOffset","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". The Control’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control\/tooltipText","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" will also scale according to this value.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control\/scale","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Control/scale":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"scale"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiftGodotRuntime7Vector2V","text":"Vector2"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The node’s scale, relative to its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"size"},{"type":"text","text":". Change this property to scale the node around its "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control\/pivotOffset"},{"type":"text","text":". The Control’s "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control\/tooltipText"},{"type":"text","text":" will also scale according to this value."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control\/scale","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/control\/scale","title":"scale","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Control/tooltipText":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"tooltipText"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The default tooltip text. The tooltip appears when the user’s mouse cursor stays idle over this control for a few moments, provided that the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control\/mouseFilter-swift.property"},{"type":"text","text":" property is not "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control\/MouseFilter-swift.enum\/ignore"},{"type":"text","text":". The time required for the tooltip to appear can be changed with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProjectSettings\/gui\/timers\/tooltipDelaySec"},{"type":"text","text":" setting."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control\/tooltipText","title":"tooltipText","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/control\/tooltiptext"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Control":{"role":"symbol","title":"Control","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Base class for all GUI controls. Adapts its position and size based on its parent control.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Control"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Control"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/control"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Control/MouseFilter-swift.enum/ignore":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The control will not receive any mouse movement input events nor mouse button input events through "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control\/_guiInput(event:)"},{"type":"text","text":". The control will also not receive the [signal mouse_entered] nor [signal mouse_exited] signals. This will not block other controls from receiving these events or firing the signals. Ignored events will not be handled automatically. If a child has "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control\/MouseFilter-swift.enum\/pass"},{"type":"text","text":" and an event was passed to this control, the event will further propagate up to the control’s parent."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/control\/mousefilter-swift.enum\/ignore","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control\/MouseFilter-swift.enum\/ignore","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ignore"}],"title":"Control.MouseFilter.ignore","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/SystemFont/multichannelSignedDistanceField":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"multichannelSignedDistanceField","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/systemfont\/multichannelsigneddistancefield","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If set to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":", glyphs of all sizes are rendered using single multichannel signed distance field generated from the dynamic font vector data."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/SystemFont\/multichannelSignedDistanceField","type":"topic","title":"multichannelSignedDistanceField"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Container":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Base class for all GUI containers."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/container","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Container","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Container","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Container","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Container"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Control/rotation":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"rotation","abstract":[{"text":"The node’s rotation around its pivot, in radians. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control\/pivotOffset","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" to change the pivot’s position.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"rotation","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/control\/rotation","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control\/rotation"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Control/pivotOffset":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/control\/pivotoffset","title":"pivotOffset","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"By default, the node’s pivot is its top-left corner. When you change its ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control\/rotation","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control\/scale","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", it will rotate or scale around this pivot. Set this property to ","type":"text"},{"code":"size","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ 2 to pivot around the Control’s center.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control\/pivotOffset","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"pivotOffset","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vector2","preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiftGodotRuntime7Vector2V","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/FontFile/oversampling":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/fontfile\/oversampling","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/FontFile\/oversampling","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"oversampling","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"oversampling","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Font oversampling factor. If set to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0.0"},{"text":", the global oversampling factor is used instead. Used by dynamic fonts only (MSDF fonts ignore oversampling).","type":"text"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Framework to write Godot Game Extensions using the Swift Programming Language."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","title":"SwiftGodot","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Control/mouseFilter-swift.property":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Controls whether the control will be able to receive mouse button input events through "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control\/_guiInput(event:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and how these events should be handled. Also controls whether the control can receive the [signal mouse_entered], and [signal mouse_exited] signals. See the constants to learn what each does."}],"title":"mouseFilter","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mouseFilter"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Control","preciseIdentifier":"s:10SwiftGodot7ControlC"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MouseFilter","preciseIdentifier":"s:10SwiftGodot7ControlC11MouseFilterO"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Control\/mo